    <p class="title is-5 mathjax">
      
        Hamiltonian Formalism for Comparing Quantum and Classical Intelligence
      
    </p>
    <p class="authors">
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Authors:</span>
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Perrier%2C+E">Elija Perrier</a>
      
    </p>
    
    <p class="abstract mathjax">
      <span class="search-hit">Abstract</span>:
      <span class="abstract-short has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2506.14456v1-abstract-short" style="display: inline;">
        &hellip;the environment. We propose a decomposition of AGI dynamics into Hamiltonian generators for core functions such as induction, reasoning, recursion, learning, measurement, and <span class="search-hit mathjax">memory</span>. This formalism aims to contribute to the development of a precise mathematical language for how quantum and classical <span class="search-hit mathjax">agents</span> differ via e&hellip;
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2506.14456v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'inline'; document.getElementById('2506.14456v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'none';">&#9661; More</a>
      </span>
      <span class="abstract-full has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2506.14456v1-abstract-full" style="display: none;">
        The prospect of AGI instantiated on quantum substrates motivates the development of mathematical frameworks that enable direct comparison of their operation in classical and quantum environments. To this end, we introduce a Hamiltonian formalism for describing classical and quantum AGI tasks as a means of contrasting their interaction with the environment. We propose a decomposition of AGI dynamics into Hamiltonian generators for core functions such as induction, reasoning, recursion, learning, measurement, and <span class="search-hit mathjax">memory</span>. This formalism aims to contribute to the development of a precise mathematical language for how quantum and classical <span class="search-hit mathjax">agents</span> differ via environmental interaction.
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2506.14456v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'none'; document.getElementById('2506.14456v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'inline';">&#9651; Less</a>
      </span>
    </p>
    

    <p class="is-size-7"><span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Submitted</span> 17 June, 2025; 
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">originally announced</span> June 2025.
      
    </p>
    
    <p class="comments is-size-7">
